        "body": "Okta is a publicly traded identity security company, founded in 2009 and headquartered in San Francisco, California, that trades on the NASDAQ under the ticker OKTA. The company describes itself as providing secure access, authentication, and automation through two platforms, Okta and Auth0, which it positions as serving employees, customers, and non-human identities alike. It describes identity as the foundation of business security and growth, and emphasizes extensibility for workforce, customer, and machine identity use cases.\n\nOn the AI side, Okta offers a product called Okta AI, categorized under Security and Identity AI, which the site describes as covering identity AI, risk-based authentication, privileged access, and identity threat detection. The company holds a significant California legal exposure profile, with 175 cases associated with that jurisdiction recorded in the site's held facts, though no specific litigation details are provided in the available data.",
